  <p>
(F) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Normal Operation Procedure</b></p>

<table style="width:95%; border-collapse: collapse;border: 1px solid #000;font-size:15px;margin-top:1cm;">
    <tr>
        <th style="border: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold; text-align:center;height: 18px;width:8%;">Sr. No.</th>
        <th style="border: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold; text-align:center;height: 18px;">Operation Procedure</th>
        <th style="border: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold; text-align:center;height: 18px;width:8%;">Action By</th>
        <th style="border: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold; text-align:center;height: 18px;width:8%;">Check</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Ensure compliance with MGL Life Saving Rules and COP requirements. Conduct site specific HIRA.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp; M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Inform Emergency control room about commencement of NRO.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of Valve V04 (size 3/4th) AG2 (size 3/4th) &amp; remove if found.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Issue work permit for confined space entry for entering steel valve chambers.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp; M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Close the valve V03 (size 4”) completely &amp; ensure Lockout &amp; Tagout of valve. Allow Jogeshwari Petrol Supply compressor to run till it trips at low suction pressure.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">6</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Connect Vent Stack and Flame arrestor at Valve AG2. Open Valve AG2 and vent the residual gas in the pipeline using a vent stack and flame arrestor.<br/>
            <b>Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3 - Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">7</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Disconnect the Flexible Hose (A-B) connected to the Jogeshwari Petrol Supply compressor. Install Blind Flange (BLRF) at point B and install Blind Flange (BLRF) with Nipple arrangement along with Vent Valve at Point A.
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">8</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Connect the nitrogen hose at V04, start Nitrogen purging by opening Valve V04 and venting from Valve AG2 &amp; Vent Valve at Point A using vent stacks with flame arrestors.<br/><br/>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">9</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Issue hot work permit. Allow construction team to cut pipeline Valve AG1 (Size 4) by cold cutting (Hacksaw). Check for trace of black powder and report appropriately.<br/>
            <b>Refer: PTW system.</b>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">10</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Complete the connectivity of new valve AG1 (size 4).</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">11</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Continue purging till 95% GIA is achieved at Valve AG2 &amp; Vent Valve at Point A and close Valve AG2 &amp; then put Blind Flange.
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">12</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Now, Close Valve AG1 and vent from Point A with Vent Stack &amp; flame arrestor. After venting, reconnect Flexible hose A-B by disconnecting Blind Flanges at both ends.
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">13</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">
            Then Open Valve V03 completely &amp; recommission the line.<br/>
            Refer: WI: O&amp;M WI 102
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">14</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Check all flanged joints for leakages with soap solution &amp; Gasco seeker.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">15</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;">Close all work permits and inform Emergency Control Room about completion of NRO.</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>
     <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;height: 25px;">16</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"> Check % of gas at valves AG2 &amp; Vent Valve at Point A. Stop Nitrogen Purging when safe limit (0 PPM) is achieved at all vent points.<br/>
            <b>Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3 - Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b></td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;text-align:center;">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td style="border: 1px solid #000;"></td>
    </tr>
  
</table>

      <div style="page-break-after: always;">
    </div>
     <table style="width:100%;">
    <tr>
        <td style="text-align:left; font-weight:bold;">
            Title: Non-Routine Operation
        </td>
        <td style="text-align:right; font-weight:bold;">
            Record No.: AIQ RE 134
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>  
    <p>(G) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Contingency Action Plan:</b></p>
   
    <p> <b style="color:red;">Passing of valve V03</b><br/>Incase of passing of Valve V03, we will need to close the Valves V01 &amp; V08 which will result into disconnection of Looping network. So in case of passing of Valve V03, inform the Emergency Control Room and abandoned the NRO and restore the valve as per the given NRO procedure.
After the NRO abandoned, downstream load will be assessed, accordingly suitable action plan will be prepared for the supply continuity. New NRO will be prepared to execute the Steel Valve Replacement AG1 mentioned in the NRO drawing.</p>
    
